# The duck's Pi, for the PC-side scripts (pi/deploy.sh, pi/watch.py, pi/twin.py --remote).
# Copy this file to .env at the repo root and fill in your own Pi. .env is git-ignored: it never goes into a commit.
# No password here: the scripts log in with the SSH key (pi/README.md, "Set up a new Pi"), and sudo on the Pi asks for its
# password in your terminal when it needs it.
DUCK_USER=pi
DUCK_HOST=duck.local
DUCK_KEY=~/.ssh/duck_ed25519
